<header class="landing-nav">
  <div class="landing-nav__inner">
    <div class="landing-nav__logo">
      <%= render "shared/logo_icon" %>
      Screenote
    </div>
    <nav class="landing-nav__links">
      <%= link_to "Sign In", new_session_path, class: "landing-nav__link" %>
      <%= link_to "Get Started", sign_up_path, class: "landing-nav__cta" %>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero__grid"></div>
  <div class="hero__glow"></div>

  <div class="hero__annotations">
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--rect hero__anno--1"></div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--rect hero__anno--2"></div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--rect hero__anno--3"></div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--pin hero__anno--4">1</div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--pin hero__anno--5">2</div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--pin hero__anno--6">3</div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--cursor hero__anno--7">
      <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M5.65 3.15l13.2 7.6-5.4 1.8-2.4 5.4z"/></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--comment hero__anno--8">Fix this padding</div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--comment hero__anno--9">Wrong color</div>
    <div class="hero__anno hero__anno--comment hero__anno--10">Align to grid</div>
  </div>

  <div class="hero__content">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">UI review for AI agents</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">
      Point at the bug.<br>
      <span class="hero__highlight">Claude</span> fixes it.
    </h1>
    <p class="hero__subtitle">
      Mark areas on your screen, write what's wrong. Your AI agent reads
      the annotations with the actual cropped image and fixes what you pointed at.
      No more describing UI issues in words.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <%= link_to "Start for Free", sign_up_path, class: "hero__btn hero__btn--primary" %>
      <a href="#how-it-works" class="hero__btn hero__btn--ghost">See How It Works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="workflow" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="workflow__inner">
    <h2 class="workflow__heading">How it works</h2>
    <div class="workflow__steps">
      <div class="workflow__step">
        <div class="workflow__step-number">01</div>
        <div class="workflow__step-icon">
          <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/>
            <circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"/>
            <path d="m21 15-5-5L5 21"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="workflow__step-title">Screenshot</h3>
        <p class="workflow__step-desc">Upload a screenshot yourself, or type <code>/screenote</code> in Claude Code and it takes one for you automatically.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow__step">
        <div class="workflow__step-number">02</div>
        <div class="workflow__step-icon">
          <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="workflow__step-title">Mark &amp; Comment</h3>
        <p class="workflow__step-desc">Draw a rectangle around the problem area, write what's wrong. Like Figma comments but for AI agents.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow__step">
        <div class="workflow__step-number">03</div>
        <div class="workflow__step-icon">
          <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 2a4 4 0 0 0-4 4c0 2 2 3 2 6h4c0-3 2-4 2-6a4 4 0 0 0-4-4z"/>
            <path d="M10 18h4"/>
            <path d="M10 22h4"/>
            <path d="M12 22v-4"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="workflow__step-title">Agent Fixes</h3>
        <p class="workflow__step-desc">Your AI reads each annotation with the cropped image region. It sees exactly what you see and fixes it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features">
  <div class="features__inner">
    <div class="features__card features__card--wide">
      <div class="features__card-label">The Problem</div>
      <h3 class="features__card-title">Describing UI bugs in words is painful. Pointing at them is natural.</h3>
      <p class="features__card-desc">
        You know what's wrong — the padding is off, the color is wrong, the layout broke.
        Instead of writing a paragraph explaining where the issue is, just draw a box around it
        and type "fix this". Your AI agent gets the cropped image region and your comment.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="features__card">
      <div class="features__card-label">Killer Feature</div>
      <h3 class="features__card-title">Agent screenshots its own work, you review, agent iterates</h3>
      <p class="features__card-desc">
        Type <code>/screenote</code> in Claude Code. The agent screenshots localhost,
        uploads it, you mark what's wrong, then the agent reads your feedback
        and fixes it. Repeat until it's perfect.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="features__card">
      <div class="features__card-label">How It Connects</div>
      <h3 class="features__card-title">MCP protocol — your agent reads annotations natively</h3>
      <p class="features__card-desc">
        No copy-pasting feedback. Your AI agent connects via Model Context Protocol
        and gets each annotation with the actual cropped screenshot region.
        It sees what you see.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-section">
  <div class="cta-section__inner">
    <h2 class="cta-section__title">Close the loop between<br>humans and AI agents.</h2>
    <p class="cta-section__subtitle">Free to start. No credit card required.</p>
    <%= link_to "Create Your First Project", sign_up_path, class: "cta-section__btn" %>
  </div>
</section>

<footer class="landing-footer">
  <div class="landing-footer__inner">
    <span class="landing-footer__brand">Screenote</span>
    <nav class="landing-footer__links">
      <%= link_to "Terms", terms_path %>
      <%= link_to "Privacy", privacy_path %>
    </nav>
    <span class="landing-footer__copy">&copy; <%= Date.current.year %></span>
  </div>
</footer>
